  "description": "Mistral AI is a French artificial intelligence company headquartered in Paris that builds frontier open-weight and commercial large language models, AI agents, and developer platforms. Founded in April 2023 by former Meta and Google DeepMind researchers Arthur Mensch, Guillaume Lample, and Timothée Lacroix, it pairs open models such as Mistral 3, Devstral, and Voxtral with enterprise products including Le Chat, Studio, Forge, and Vibe. Mistral raised a €3 billion Series D led by Samsung Electronics in September 2026 at a post-money valuation above €21 billion, the largest equity round ever by a European technology company, and operates across 20 countries serving 125+ global enterprises.",
